{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "foundry-doctor",
          "version": "v0.0.0-test",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/ruairispain/copilot-web/tree/main/foundry-doctor",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "FND-CFG-001",
              "name": "FND-CFG-001",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Valid YAML, duplicate-key detection and compatible azure.ai.* schema"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "azure.yaml must parse as YAML with unique mapping keys and conform to the published azd schema (v1.0) for the azure.ai.* service hosts: azure.ai.project, azure.ai.agent, azure.ai.connection, azure.ai.toolbox, azure.ai.skill, azure.ai.routine (and azure.ai.eval). Constraints checked are those the schema states as required, const, enum, type or \"not\": top-level name pattern, services with at least one entry, host required on every service, project required on azure.ai.agent, prompt agents requiring model and instructions, azure.ai.project forbidding project/runtime/docker/image/config, and the unsupported voice authoring shapes (modelType hosted_agent, targetAgent). Unknown properties are not errors because the schema allows additional properties. Also reports when the declared requiredVersions are older than the extension versions the schema was verified against."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Fix the YAML syntax or the reported schema violation. Add the yaml-language-server schema comment to azure.yaml so the editor flags the same errors, and install azure.ai.agents and azure.ai.projects at the versions declared in requiredVersions. See https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/agents/concepts/azure-yaml-reference",
                "markdown": "Fix the YAML syntax or the reported schema violation. Add the yaml-language-server schema comment to azure.yaml so the editor flags the same errors, and install azure.ai.agents and azure.ai.projects at the versions declared in requiredVersions.\n\n[Documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/agents/concepts/azure-yaml-reference)"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/agents/concepts/azure-yaml-reference",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "foundry-doctor",
                  "must-have",
                  "operations",
                  "platform"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "FND-ENV-001",
              "name": "FND-ENV-001",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Environments do not unintentionally share resource groups"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Two azd environments of the same project (for example dev and prod) should not resolve to the same resource group. azd documents one resource group per environment for isolation; azure.yaml resourceGroup overrides the name used for provisioning, and a value without an environment-specific component makes every environment target the same group, so tearing down or redeploying one environment affects the other."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Give each environment its own resource group, for example by including the environment name in the group name (resourceGroup: rg-${AZURE_ENV_NAME}), or record an explicit suppression with a reason and expiry when sharing is intentional. See https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/developer/azure-developer-cli/environments-overview",
                "markdown": "Give each environment its own resource group, for example by including the environment name in the group name (resourceGroup: rg-${AZURE\\_ENV\\_NAME}), or record an explicit suppression with a reason and expiry when sharing is intentional.\n\n[Documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/developer/azure-developer-cli/environments-overview)"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/developer/azure-developer-cli/environments-overview",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "foundry-doctor",
                  "must-have",
                  "operations"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "originalUriBaseIds": {
        "%SRCROOT%": {
          "uri": "./"
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": true,
          "exitCode": 1,
          "toolExecutionNotifications": [
            {
              "level": "note",
              "message": {
                "text": "Skipped FND-NET-001: synthetic-infrastructure (missing capability: compiled ARM template). Skipped is not passed."
              },
              "descriptor": {
                "id": "FND-NET-001"
              },
              "associatedRule": {
                "id": "FND-NET-001"
              },
              "properties": {
                "missingCapability": "compiled ARM template",
                "reason": "synthetic-infrastructure",
                "skipped": true
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "FND-CFG-001",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "azure.yaml has a problem"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "azure.yaml",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 3,
                  "startColumn": 1,
                  "endLine": 3,
                  "endColumn": 2
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "api",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "api",
                  "kind": "service"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "foundryDoctor/v1": "fp1:b87a6f615847f99b96d6e2698248afd0",
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "36b794d184b08c4e:1"
          },
          "properties": {
            "basis": [
              "platform"
            ],
            "confidence": "certain",
            "profile": "foundry-test",
            "ruleVersion": 1,
            "severity": "error"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "FND-ENV-001",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "an environment value is missing"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "azure.yaml",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 3,
                  "startColumn": 1,
                  "endLine": 3,
                  "endColumn": 2
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "api",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "api",
                  "kind": "service"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "foundryDoctor/v1": "fp1:4973db290995ad26b2efbd7382701a3c",
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "4389cd9b44e5c72c:1"
          },
          "properties": {
            "basis": [
              "operations"
            ],
            "confidence": "certain",
            "profile": "foundry-test",
            "ruleVersion": 1,
            "severity": "warning"
          }
        }
      ],
      "properties": {
        "hidden": 0,
        "profile": "foundry-test"
      }
    }
  ]
}
